.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd October 16, 2026
.Dt GETVFSSTAT 2
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm getvfsstat
.Nd list the mounted file systems
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/statvfs.h
.Ft int
.Fn getvfsstat "struct statvfs *buf" "size_t bufsize" "int flags"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn getvfsstat
fills
.Fa buf
with a
.Vt struct statvfs
for each mounted file system, in the order they were mounted, as many as
.Fa bufsize
bytes hold.
With
.Fa buf
a null pointer it fills nothing and counts them.
.Pp
On OxideBSD, as on
.Nx ,
.Vt struct statvfs
carries, after the members
.Xr statvfs 3
describes, the file system's names:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
char f_fstypename[VFS_NAMELEN];   /* its type: oxfs, tmpfs, procfs */
char f_mntonname[VFS_MNAMELEN];   /* where it is mounted */
char f_mntfromname[VFS_MNAMELEN]; /* what it is mounted from */
.Ed
.Pp
.Xr statvfs 3
and
.Xr fstatvfs 3
fill them too.
.Pp
.Fa flags
is
.Dv ST_WAIT
or
.Dv ST_NOWAIT ;
every record is fresh either way.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The number of records filled (or, with a null
.Fa buf ,
the number of mounted file systems); \-1 on error, with
.Va errno
set.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EFAULT
.Fa buf
points outside the address space.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
.Fa flags
is neither
.Dv ST_WAIT
nor
.Dv ST_NOWAIT .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nmount 2 ,
.Xr statvfs 3 ,
.Xr mount 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Fn getvfsstat
first appeared in
.Nx 3.0 ,
replacing
.Fn getfsstat .
In OxideBSD it is system call 587, part of the VFS (OxideBSD-doc
.Pa VFS.md
\(sc4.6).
